      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Cardiac tamponade due to coronary artery rupture, as a consequence of blunt trauma, is a rare but usually fatal condition. We successfully obtained primary hemostasis with emergency room thoracotomy, followed by delayed definitive treatment of the ruptured right coronary artery ostium in a motor vehicle accident victim with multifocal hemorrhagic lesions. Survival of patients with the described serious trauma has not been reported, and we discuss herein our treatment strategy."},
